Line 63: Escaped '%' in line: A computational study of fluidic counterflow thrust vectoring was conducted, utilizing the PAB3D computational fluid dynamics code with two-equation turbulence closure and Reynolds stress modeling. The study validated computational results against experimental data and explored the physics of counterflow-induced thrust vectoring. It was revealed that effective vectoring can be achieved with less than 1\\\% secondary flow requirements. Insights into shear layer dynamics and pressure gradients were presented, offering implications for improved control in multi-functional propulsion systems.
